hy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17457, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LgMtUp6M6WaDzBPXdsLwrR", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["honor_retry_after", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17457, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LgMtUp6M6WaDzBPXdsLwrR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21072, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What went wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been marked unhealthy in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0 and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. Opening it paged the on-call engineer. It also notes that someone needs to find what broke v2.3.1 before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01H7cntaaCMXTAYrgnoqaUmo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LsSVEWsSkT5FkwcN5RxaPQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012Zs6dAWnMhb1iJrUjCstDR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0117ayaLh9ycALCUxh8ktGzo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Q9k9RNDh5HTrhxsJnjbsv8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LgMtUp6M6WaDzBPXdsLwrR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What went wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been marked unhealthy in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0 and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. Opening it paged the on-call engineer. It also notes that someone needs to find what broke v2.3.1 before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}